{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1208905-new-2e-sas-material-or","id":1208905,"title":"New 2E. SAS material... or?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-19T09:09:32-07:00","id":1208905,"title":"New 2E. SAS material... or?","content":"One struggle I have experienced with 2E. is that there is very little pre-written material for Chronicles. For example, I never played much of Werewolf: The Forsaken 1st Edition so when I started prepping to run Second Edition, I didn't have much of a feel of &quot;What does a werewolf pack do from day to day? What problems do they have to face on a regular basis? How should a Forsaken game -feel-? How are the writers intending this game to be played?&quot;<br /> <br /> I do have access to some SAS modules for 1 edition game lines, but after reviewing some of them, it seems like some of the foundational aspects of the game lines have changed, and they seem at odds with the new editions. (Not all of them, but some.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I know that Onyx Path is focusing more on tangible content for the new lines and is focusing more on getting the 2E books out... but... I would instantly buy a new SAS for a Chronicles game line and I think it would help groups utilize the books easier.<br /> <br /> If new SAS modules are out of the question, can we get a community portal on DriveThruRPG for community released modules? Is there a downside to this that I am not seeing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1310,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1310-samare","user":"Samare","date":". 04-19-2018, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1310-samare","name":"Samare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1310_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T09:57:21-07:00","id":1208928,"title":"","content":"The future of SAS as a thing is unknown. We're more likely to see quickstart style modules (the Reap the Whirlwind for VtR 2e).<br /> <br /> A community portal is hard to speculate about, because that would ultimately be in White Wolf's hands, no Onyx Path's hands; including what is acceptable content to post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}